When the same query is searched again on the same provider with the
same filters, the new record wins: [[add_query_provider_pair]] keeps the
first record of a key, and the current results are added before the
previous session's.  A run with other filters is another search and
leaves the earlier record alone (\cref{sec:search-record-key}).
That is right when the re-run answered---it is the newer answer---but
wrong when it failed.  Re-running a query while a provider is down would
otherwise overwrite \enquote{12 hits} with \enquote{failed}, although the
twelve papers from the earlier run are still in the session.  So an
earlier record that answered replaces a failed re-run of the same pair.
The failure itself is not lost from view: it was reported when it
happened, and the session keeps the answer that its papers came from.

