\paragraph{Unreadable session files.}
[[read_session_file]] turns every way a file can fail to parse into one
exception that names the file.  Callers that only read ([[sessions
show]], [[llm status]], \dots) keep the old behaviour through
[[load_session]]: a warning and \enquote{session not found}.  Callers that
would \emph{write} the session afterwards must not treat it as missing,
so they pass [[strict=True]] and let the error stop them
(\cref{sec:review-create-strict}).

<<review data structures>>=
class SessionFileError(Exception):
    """A session file exists but cannot be read or parsed."""

    def __init__(self, path: Path, cause: Exception):
        self.path = path
        self.cause = cause
        super().__init__(f"Cannot read session file {path}: {cause}")
@

