\subsection{Search parameters and research context}

Sessions built before query-provider pairs were recorded only have the
base query and the provider list, so the pairs are reconstructed from
those when missing.

<<review report generation>>=
def get_query_provider_pairs(session: ReviewSession) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:
    """Return query/provider pairs with backward-compatible fallback."""
    if session.query_provider_pairs:
        return session.query_provider_pairs
    return [(session.query, provider) for provider in session.providers]


def provider_queries_differ(session: ReviewSession) -> bool:
    """Whether any provider-specific query differs from the base query."""
    pairs = get_query_provider_pairs(session)
    return any(query != session.query for query, _ in pairs)
@

A report built on a session where a provider failed must not let the
reader assume that provider was searched.  [[search_outcomes]] pairs
each query and provider with the label of what the search returned
([[hits_label]], \cref{sec:search-result-error}): a count, or
\enquote{failed} with the reason.  Records from before outcomes were
stored---and sessions so old that they have no records at all---get an
empty label, since we do not know.  The provider table then appears
also when every provider ran the base query but one of them failed, and
it gains a hits column whenever at least one outcome is known; a report
built from an old session therefore looks exactly as it did.

A query can also be run twice on one provider with different filters,
say once over the full text and once with [[--in title-abstract]]
(\cref{sec:search-record-key}).  Those are two searches with two
counts, and a table of query and provider alone would show two rows
that look the same.  So each row carries the search's filter flags,
written as [[scholar search]] takes them ([[filter_flags]],
\cref{sec:filter-flags} in the [[scholar]] module), in a column that
appears when any search had filters; and the table appears whenever two
searches share their query and provider ([[search_table_needed]]),
since only the table tells them apart.

<<review report generation>>=
def search_outcomes(
    session: ReviewSession,
) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str]]:
    """Return `(query, provider, flags, outcome label)` for each search.

    `flags` are the filter flags of the search, as `scholar search`
    takes them (empty when it had none).
    """
    if not session.search_records:
        return [(q, p, "", "") for q, p in get_query_provider_pairs(session)]
    return [
        (
            r.query, r.provider, " ".join(filter_flags(r.filters)),
            hits_label(
                r.hits, r.error, r.retries,
                ranked=is_ranked_provider(r.provider),
            ),
        )
        for r in session.search_records
    ]


def searches_share_query(session: ReviewSession) -> bool:
    """Whether two recorded searches have the same query and provider."""
    pairs = [(r.query, r.provider) for r in session.search_records]
    return len(pairs) != len(set(pairs))


def search_table_needed(session: ReviewSession) -> bool:
    """Whether the report needs its table of provider searches."""
    return (
        provider_queries_differ(session)
        or any_search_failed(session)
        or searches_share_query(session)
    )


def any_search_failed(session: ReviewSession) -> bool:
    """Whether any recorded search failed."""
    return any(r.error for r in session.search_records)
@

The research context and the search parameters exist in a Markdown and a
\LaTeX{} flavour because the synthesis offers both output formats. The
\LaTeX{} builders take the heading command as a parameter for the reason
given above; the provider table only appears when at least one provider
ran a query different from the base query, since otherwise it would
repeat the base query once per provider---or when a search failed,
since the failure must be visible either way, or when two searches
share their query and provider, since only the table's filters column
tells them apart.

<<review report generation>>=
def build_research_context_markdown(
    session: ReviewSession,
    heading_level: int = 3,
) -> list[str]:
    """Build the research context section as Markdown lines."""
    if not session.research_context:
        return []

    heading = "#" * heading_level
    return [
        f"{heading} Research Context",
        "",
        session.research_context,
        "",
    ]


def build_search_parameters_markdown(
    session: ReviewSession,
    heading_level: int = 3,
) -> list[str]:
    """Build search parameters (including executed queries) as Markdown lines."""
    heading = "#" * heading_level
    providers = ", ".join(session.providers)

    lines: list[str] = [
        f"{heading} Search Parameters",
        "",
        f"- Base query: {session.query}",
        f"- Providers: {providers}",
        "",
    ]

    if search_table_needed(session):
        heading2 = "#" * (heading_level + 1)
        outcomes = search_outcomes(session)
        with_hits = any(label for *_, label in outcomes)
        with_flags = any(flags for _, _, flags, _ in outcomes)
        columns = ["Provider", "Query"]
        columns += ["Filters"] if with_flags else []
        columns += ["Hits"] if with_hits else []
        lines.extend([
            f"{heading2} Provider-specific queries",
            "",
            "| " + " | ".join(columns) + " |",
            "|" + " --- |" * len(columns),
        ])
        for query, provider, flags, label in outcomes:
            cells = [provider, query]
            cells += [f"`{flags}`" if flags else ""] if with_flags else []
            cells += [label] if with_hits else []
            lines.append("| " + " | ".join(cells) + " |")
        lines.append("")

    return lines


def latex_flags(flags: str) -> str:
    """Typeset command-line flags in typewriter, keeping `--` two hyphens."""
    if not flags:
        return ""
    return r"\texttt{" + escape_latex(flags).replace("--", "-{}-") + "}"


def build_research_context_latex(
    session: ReviewSession,
    heading_command: str = r"\section",
) -> list[str]:
    """Build the research context section as LaTeX lines."""
    if not session.research_context:
        return []

    lines = [f"{heading_command}{{Research Context}}"]
    lines.extend(markdown_to_latex(session.research_context).splitlines())
    lines.append("")
    return lines


def build_search_parameters_latex(
    session: ReviewSession,
    heading_command: str = r"\section",
) -> list[str]:
    """Build search parameters (including executed queries) as LaTeX lines."""
    providers = ", ".join(session.providers)

    lines: list[str] = [f"{heading_command}{{Search Parameters}}", ""]
    lines.extend(
        [
            r"\begin{description}",
            f"\\item[Base query] {escape_latex(session.query)}",
            f"\\item[Providers] {escape_latex(providers)}",
            r"\end{description}",
            "",
        ]
    )

    if search_table_needed(session):
        outcomes = search_outcomes(session)
        with_hits = any(label for *_, label in outcomes)
        with_flags = any(flags for _, _, flags, _ in outcomes)
        spec = "lp{8cm}" if with_hits else "lp{10cm}"
        header = ["Provider", "Query"]
        if with_flags:
            spec = "lp{6cm}p{3.5cm}" if with_hits else "lp{7cm}p{3.5cm}"
            header.append("Filters")
        if with_hits:
            spec += "p{3.5cm}"
            header.append("Hits")
        lines.extend(
            [
                f"{sub_heading(heading_command)}{{Provider-specific queries}}",
                rf"\begin{{longtable}}{{{spec}}}",
                r"\toprule",
                " & ".join(header) + r" \\",
                r"\midrule",
            ]
        )
        for query, provider, flags, label in outcomes:
            cells = [escape_latex(provider), escape_latex(query)]
            if with_flags:
                cells.append(latex_flags(flags))
            if with_hits:
                cells.append(escape_latex(label))
            lines.append(" & ".join(cells) + r" \\")
        lines.extend(
            [
                r"\bottomrule",
                r"\end{longtable}",
                "",
            ]
        )

    return lines
