@dataclass
class AuditRow:
    """One row of the audit table: a unique paper and its reason."""

    title: str
    year: str
    providers: list[str]
    status: DecisionStatus
    reason: str
    order: int
    excluded: bool = False   # discarded despite a bearing category
@

Three facts about how decisions are recorded shape the cited rule.
First, [[sessions decide -t]] appends to a row's tags, so a human who
keeps an LLM-classified [[supports-claim]] paper under a theme leaves
both tags on it; looking only at the first tag would file the paper
under the category and count no cited rows at all. The rule therefore
splits the tags into category tags, note tags and theme tags and takes
the theme from the last group. Second, an LLM keep is a candidate, not
a citation: only a decision a human made (or reviewed) counts as cited,
which is also what the [[decision_source]] column of the CSV export
says. Third, when the caller names its themes with [[--theme]], that
list is an allowlist: any other tag that is neither a category nor a
known note is shown as a note, so a stray tag cannot pass for a theme.
Without the list, every tag that is not a category or a note is a
theme. Notes are appended in parentheses to whatever reason the row
has; a row with only notes is filed among the \enquote{other} rows.

When a row carries several category tags, the \emph{last} one is the
decision: tags accumulate in the order they were given, so a reviewer
who changes an LLM's \enquote{supports} to \enquote{false hit} leaves
both, and taking the first once counted an explicitly rejected paper as
supporting evidence in a published appendix. The confidence is shown
for the rows whose category is the machine's: unreviewed LLM decisions
and the ones a human confirmed as they stood. A human who changed the
decision owns the new label, so no confidence goes with it. Finally, a
theme that merely repeats the word \enquote{cited} adds nothing and is
not repeated.

The caption promises a confidence for every machine-classified row, so
such a row recorded without one---[[sessions decide --source llm]]
without [[--confidence]], or a session from before the classifier
stored it---says so with a localised \enquote{n/a} instead of looking
like a human row. An empty cell would be read as \enquote{nobody
asked}, which is exactly what the reader cannot check.

The category is the classification, but the status is the decision,
and the decision wins (issue~\#89). A row whose final status is
discarded is never listed as cited, supporting or qualifying, whatever
its category says: the reviewer, or the model, looked at the paper and
excluded it, and counting it as evidence for the claim in a published
appendix is exactly the mistake the issue reported. Such a row keeps
its category in the reason, marked as excluded, but sorts among the
\enquote{other} rows, so [[--bearing-only]] never lists it and the
caption counts it separately. The adjacent and off-topic categories do
not bear on the claim, so a discarded row there is simply what it says.

<<review report generation>>=
def audit_category(tags: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """Return the deciding (last) audit category among `tags`, if any."""
    return next((t for t in reversed(tags) if t in AUDIT_CATEGORIES), None)


def audit_excluded(decision: ReviewDecision) -> bool:
    """Tell whether a bearing category was overruled by a discard."""
    category = audit_category(decision.tags)
    return (
        decision.status == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
        and category is not None
        and AUDIT_CATEGORIES[category] <= AUDIT_ORDER_BEARING
    )


def audit_reason(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    strings: dict,
) -> tuple[str, int]:
    """Return the reason label and sort order for `decision`."""
    tags = list(decision.tags)
    notes = strings["notes"]
    category = audit_category(tags)
    note_texts = [notes[t] for t in tags if t in notes]
    if theme_names:
        theme_tags = [t for t in tags if t in theme_names]
        note_texts += [
            escape_latex(t) for t in tags
            if t not in AUDIT_CATEGORIES and t not in notes
            and t not in theme_names
        ]
    else:
        theme_tags = [
            t for t in tags if t not in AUDIT_CATEGORIES and t not in notes
        ]
    human_decision = decision.source != ReviewSource.LLM_UNREVIEWED
    kept = decision.status == DecisionStatus.KEPT
    machine_label = decision.source == ReviewSource.LLM_UNREVIEWED or (
        decision.source == ReviewSource.LLM_REVIEWED
        and not decision.is_example
    )
    confidence = ""
    if machine_label and decision.llm_confidence is not None:
        confidence = f" ({decision.llm_confidence:.2f})"
    elif machine_label:
        confidence = f" ({strings['no_confidence']})"

    if decision.status == DecisionStatus.PENDING:
        return strings["pending"], AUDIT_ORDER_PENDING
    if kept and human_decision and theme_tags:
        theme = theme_names.get(theme_tags[0], theme_tags[0])
        label = f"\\emph{{{strings['cited']}}}"
        if theme.casefold() != strings["cited"].casefold():
            label += ": " + escape_latex(theme)
        order = AUDIT_ORDER_CITED
    elif kept and human_decision and not tags:
        label, order = f"\\emph{{{strings['cited']}}}", AUDIT_ORDER_CITED
    elif audit_excluded(decision):
        label = f"{strings[category]}{confidence}, {strings['excluded']}"
        order = AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER
    elif category is not None:
        label = strings[category] + confidence
        order = AUDIT_CATEGORIES[category]
    elif note_texts:
        return "; ".join(note_texts), AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER
    elif not tags:
        return strings["pending"], AUDIT_ORDER_PENDING
    else:
        return escape_latex(tags[0]) + confidence, AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER
    if note_texts:
        label += " (" + "; ".join(note_texts) + ")"
    return label, order
@

